threading:
	concurrent.futures
	thread pool executor
	thread class:
		pool -> list of threads
		each thread executes a target method
		scheduleing overhead, scheduleing done by OS, OS naively interleavs in the assembly code, 
			- to prevent the invalid state due to interleaving:
				- lock on the level of individual bytecode by python interpreter -> Global interpreter lock(GIL)
				- thread contend for the GIL
				
		-- import lock -> lock on import of modules
		
		threads operate on a common memory
		interleaving may happen on one thread reading the data and other mutating it, first thread read a stale data
		interleaving on reading data -> clobbered read
		
		so we offload the interleaving to the application level(we lock instead of OS GIL)"from threading import Lock"
		
		
		
multiprocessing:
	process is fundamental unit of isolation
	processes has each it's own memory and GIL, contention only inside a process, not between process
	data in multiprocessing is movable and copyable -> picklable -> can be moved around
		generators, file handlers, etc are not picklable
	CPU bound -> only if the data movement between processes is low
		solved by multiprocessing.shared_memory
		
	
